/-
# Kitaoka 1993, Proposition 1.6.3: generators of $O'(V)$ for isotropic $V$

**Source.** Y. Kitaoka, *Arithmetic of Quadratic Forms* (1993), §1.6, Proposition 1.6.3, p. 30 (printed page).

**Setting.** The repository's orthogonal groups are matrix groups: for a quadratic form $Q$ in $n$ variables with
coefficients in a number field $F$ and a field $K \supseteq F$ of characteristic $0$, $O(V)(K)$ is
`Lattices.orthGroup Q K`, $\tau_x$ is the symmetry `Lattices.symm Q K x`, and $O'(V)(K)$ (the kernel of the spinor norm
on $O^+(V)(K)$, Kitaoka §1.6) is `Lattices.spinorKernel Q K` (shown equal to the kernel of the spinor norm in
`Lattices/SpinorNorm.lean`). Kitaoka states the proposition over an arbitrary field; the statement below is the case of
a space $V = K^n$ whose form has coefficients in a number field $F \subseteq K$ and $\operatorname{char} K = 0$, which is
the generality of these objects in the repository. Isotropic means $Q(x) = 0$ for some nonzero $x \in K^n$.
-/
import QuadFormsKB.Lattices.SpinorKernel

open QuadFormsKB.Lattices

noncomputable section

namespace QuadFormsKB.Kitaoka

/-- **Kitaoka 1993, Proposition 1.6.3** (p. 30), *stated*: if $V$ is a regular isotropic quadratic space, then
$O'(V)$ is generated by the products $\tau_x\tau_y$ with $Q(x) = Q(y) \ne 0$. (Over $K \supseteq F$, $\operatorname{char}
K = 0$, $Q$ with coefficients in the number field $F$; see the module docstring.) -/
@[kb "kitaoka1993" "§1.6, Prop. 1.6.3, p. 30"]
def Proposition163 : Prop :=
  ∀ (F : Type) [Field F] [NumberField F] (n : ℕ) (Q : QuadForm F n) (K : Type) [Field K] [Algebra F K]
    [CharZero K], Q.Nondegenerate → (∃ x : Fin n → K, x ≠ 0 ∧ Q.evalIn K x = 0) →
    spinorKernel Q K = Subgroup.closure
      {g | ∃ x y : Fin n → K, Q.evalIn K x = Q.evalIn K y ∧ Q.evalIn K x ≠ 0 ∧ g = symm Q K x * symm Q K y}

end QuadFormsKB.Kitaoka
